---
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What types of business processes can you automate?',
    a: 'Processes that follow a repeatable pattern: responding to enquiries, routing requests, booking appointments, moving data between tools, sorting email, follow up sequences and research tasks. If a person does the same steps every time something happens, there is usually a workflow in it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you integrate the tools my business already uses?',
    a: 'In most cases, yes. Tools with an API or webhooks can usually be connected, and n8n has ready made integrations for many common business apps. I check each tool early in the project so there are no surprises about what is possible.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When should a workflow use AI instead of conventional automation?',
    a: 'When a step needs judgement on unstructured information, such as understanding a message, classifying a request or extracting details from text. When the rule is clear, plain logic is cheaper, faster and more predictable, so that is what I use.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you work with an existing n8n workflow?',
    a: 'Yes. I can review an existing workflow, fix what is breaking, improve its error handling and extend it with new steps or integrations.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you approach testing, errors and ongoing maintenance?',
    a: 'Every workflow is tested with normal cases and with the awkward ones: missing data, failed services and unexpected inputs. Errors are caught and reported instead of failing silently, and anything uncertain is passed to a person. After launch, workflows can be monitored and refined as needs change.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does a typical automation project begin?',
    a: 'With a conversation about the process you want to improve. We map how it works today, agree what a good outcome looks like and identify the tools involved. From there I propose a system design and scope before building anything.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="border-t border-line bg-ink" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container-x section-y">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-4" data-reveal>
        <p class="label text-lime">FAQ</p>
        <h2 id="faq-title" class="display mt-4 text-[clamp(2.6rem,5.5vw,4.75rem)]">Good questions.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:100ms">
        {
          faqs.map((item) => (
            <details class="faq group border-t border-line last:border-b">
              <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 text-left">
                <span class="font-display text-xl leading-snug font-semibold [font-stretch:85%] sm:text-[1.45rem]">{item.q}</span>
                <span class="mt-0.5 flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line transition-all duration-300 group-open:rotate-45 group-open:border-lime group-open:bg-lime group-open:text-ink">
                  <Icon name="plus" size={16} />
                </span>
              </summary>
              <p class="max-w-2xl pr-12 pb-7 leading-relaxed text-paper/75">{item.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
